        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Fix ACP Discord thread spawns",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\nACP thread spawns from an existing Discord thread were losing the Discord parent channel context. That made sessions_spawn(runtime=\"acp\", thread=true) try to bind/create a child thread from the current thread context instead of creating a sibling thread under the parent Discord channel, producing thread_binding_invalid in real Discord use.\n\n## Summary\n- propagate Discord thread parent context through embedded runs into sessions_spawn\n- pass the parent conversation id into ACP thread binding resolution\n- forward gateway HTTP tool invocation thread-parent headers into sessions_spawn so ACP children can create sibling Discord threads from existing Discord threads\n\n## Evidence\n- npm test -- --run src/gateway/tools-invoke-http.test.ts\n- npm test -- --run src/agents/acp-spawn.test.ts\n- npm test -- --run extensions/discord/src/monitor/thread-bindings.lifecycle.test.ts\n- pnpm tsgo:core\n- live diagnosis before the fix reproduced thread_binding_invalid when calling sessions_spawn(runtime=\"acp\", thread=true) from inside a Discord thread",
